    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because the cube root is real, \\[ \\left(-\\frac1{125}\\right)^{\\frac{2}{3}} =\\left(-\\frac15\\right)^2=\\frac1{25}. \\] The negative exponent takes the reciprocal, giving \\(25.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
